# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "An interior separator takes the ink of the segment it opens"

# RULED 2026-10-08 (the texture pass, twice over): the dialect's addresses carry no underline, so
# every interior separator stacks the ink of the segment it opens rather than reading as plain
# punctuation. This is the control for the whole arc — if a future change ever un-stacks one of
# these companions, this file reds rather than the operator's own eyes catching it a third time.
#
# Pass one: a scheme run paints as one colour; the authority's ':'/'@' take the role/place's ink;
# the root's two dots each take the ink of the leaf they open; a path slash takes the path text's
# own two-level ink.
#
# Pass two (the operator's Gruvbox finding): `support.type` alone shared a colour with the bare
# `entity.name` the authority falls back to in 18 of 65 bundled themes. `support.constant.scheme.lar`
# stacked innermost on the scheme word AND its separator drops that to 4/65, measured in
# LEDGER-3.0.0.md. The query joined the ruling too: `?`/`&` take the key's ink; `=` and the value
# (quoted or bare) carry a new honest family, `markup.other.value.lar`, chosen because every
# painting alternative regressed an already-distinct pair.

x lar://claude:scryer@lararium/a.b.c/path
